This crate (`symphonia-codec-gsm`) is a pure-Rust GSM 06.10 full-rate speech decoder (also the
Microsoft "GSM 6.10" WAVE variant, tag 0x0031). It is licensed under the Mozilla Public License,
v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

The algorithm and the constants (`src/synth.rs`: LAR decoding table MIC/B/INVA, the long-term
gain table QLB, the APCM normalisation table FAC, the integer arithmetic primitives) are those of
ETSI EN 300 961 / GSM 06.10 clause 4 (the fixed-point reference description), written with the
structure of the `libgsm` library by Jutta Degener and Carsten Bormann (Technische Universitaet
Berlin; licence retained below) as the reference for the exact operation order and saturation
behaviour. The APCM inverse-quantisation table that FFmpeg
(`libavcodec/gsmdec_data.c`, LGPL-2.1+) stores precomputed is computed here from the clause 4
formulas instead; the output was verified bit-for-bit against both FFmpeg's `gsm`/`gsm_ms`
decoders and libgsm.

